|term[resolution-engine] :status settled :defined-by def-cardinality-and-resolution :anchor engine-and-perspective
  :word resolution-engine
  :synonyms [engine]
  What performs resolution — never a property of the act itself.
  |invariants
    - Resolves zero or more [[term/reference-act]]
    - Relative to exactly one [[term/perspective]]
    - Owes the six obligations: typed outcomes; descriptors preserved; never a silent best-guess; fetch-verification when carried; weak resolution disclosed ([[DECISIONS#d6-found-but-weakly|D6 found-but-weakly]]); zero only from a completed perspective ([[DECISIONS#d7-completed-perspective|D7 completed-perspective]])
  |note :audience maintainer
    Store-model candidate identity: a bound store composition IS an engine (disc-store-composition-model).
